derivations.claim:
Decompose the force integrand as $\overline{z_k}d_k-\overline{ho_k}
abla_xa_k=\overline{(z_k-ho_k)}
abla_xa_k+\overline{z_k}(\mathfrak d_k-
abla_xa_k)+\overline{z_k}(d_k-\mathfrak d_k)$. By [F3], [F4], the given residual bound $H_k$, and $\|
abla_xa_k\|_2=|\kappa_k|$ from [F5], its norm is at most $Q[|\kappa_k|A_k+(1+A_k)B_k+(1+A_k)H_k]$. Multiply by $|q_i|c_k$ and sum to prove the uncorrected force bound.

Where the energy-gradient derivative exists, [F7] gives $
abla_{x_i}C_M=q_i^2\sum_kc_k\operatorname{Re}(\overline{b_k(t_i)}
abla_xb_k(t_i))$. By step 2.1 this is also the finite cyclic-kernel expression displayed in the Statement. Subtracting this gradient from that of $E_M$ yields the displayed corrected force. At a $P=2$ knot the same algebra defines the selected corrected branch, without claiming it is a gradient. Put $Q_i=Q-|q_i|=\sum_{j
e i}|q_j|$, $z'_k=z_k-q_ib_k(t_i)$, and $ho'_k=ho_k-q_ia_k(t_i)$. Since $\operatorname{Re}(\overline{a_k}
abla_xa_k)=\operatorname{Re}(-i\kappa_k)=0$, the exact force is unchanged when $ho_k$ is replaced by $ho'_k$. The finite sums and [F3] give $|z'_k-ho'_k|\le Q_iA_k$ and $|z'_k|\le Q_i(1+A_k)$. Repeating the force decomposition in step 1.4 with these primed coefficients and $H_k=0$ proves the corrected force bound.

For each reciprocal mode, [F6] gives $
abla_{x_i}\sigma_k=-iq_i\kappa_k a_k(t_i)$. In real and imaginary coordinates, $
abla|\sigma_k|^2=2\operatorname{Re}(\overline{\sigma_k}
abla\sigma_k)$, so differentiating a finite reciprocal partial energy gives $q_i\sum_kc_k\operatorname{Re}(\overline{\sigma_k}
abla_xa_k(t_i))$. Step 1.2 justifies passage to the full sum. The constant self term has zero derivative. Negating the real gradient in step 2.2 and this reciprocal gradient gives the force formula in the Statement; opposite reciprocal modes are conjugate pairs, so their sum is real.

Differentiating $C_M= rac12\sum_jq_j^2\sum_kc_k(|b_k(t_j)|^2-1)$ with respect to $x_i$ gives $
abla_{x_i}C_M=q_i^2\sum_kc_k\operatorname{Re}(\overline{b_k(t_i)}
abla_xb_k(t_i))$. Hence $-
abla_{x_i}(E_M-C_M)=-q_i\sum_kc_k\operatorname{Re}(\overline{z_k-q_ib_k(t_i)}
abla_xb_k(t_i))$, the corrected force formula.

